{"posts":[{"id":"aboutcompression_p13_301","t":"H4 yen","a":"Oedipus99","d":"","n":"#301","p":13,"im":["563075d2a02cafb879dc4e37fa1c367bd1c450bc"],"m":301},{"id":"aboutcompression_p13_302","t":"GU Daily Does this look like there is cp forming that could lead to a bearish move?","a":"Oedipus99","d":"","n":"#302","p":13,"im":["f8e8822b4aabd1fca38a8bce54b603794e81cacb"],"m":302},{"id":"aboutcompression_p13_303","t":"There is a few instances of cp here but this chart is more to show how price responded to the rectangles I drew in last night (in a previous post in this thread). Seems text book to me. All comments welcome. eur/aud M15","a":"Oedipus99","d":"","n":"#303","p":13,"im":["0c3e5235ec53b5fab5b6422cf08eda98f5517a16"],"m":303},{"id":"aboutcompression_p13_304","t":"I guess this answers my, is GU bearish question.","a":"Oedipus99","d":"","n":"#304","p":13,"im":["a2a36ab2809743925246bb9bcaa614b4a65892e9"],"m":304},{"id":"aboutcompression_p13_305","t":"Be interesting to see what happens next.","a":"Oedipus99","d":"","n":"#305","p":13,"im":["e696cd459bc683b3916545e543af4a688dad8d64","f9b79352df37dbb1d4ab7f481e518ebc63c18cf3"],"m":305},{"id":"aboutcompression_p13_306","t":"Monthly Euro examples of cp. I think I'm getting a handle on this but will wait for comments before going on to the next homework.","a":"Oedipus99","d":"","n":"#306","p":13,"im":["143d0039b3d8e16aca2b24fc681e234f5eb77fa3","5ea47199c685f76bf3f0f57c2c47569ad1bed5d5"],"m":306},{"id":"aboutcompression_p13_307","t":"2 GBP/JPY 4 hr tf charts showing CPLQ (Liquidity)","a":"AlexC","d":"","n":"#307","p":13,"im":["52421f4e9a47411a5269d35af37746df0c8b2b39","70c64f9b0303b7a3eddeceb10d9d59d7772f02f5"],"m":307},{"id":"aboutcompression_p13_308","t":"AlexC wrote: 2 GBP/JPY 4 hr tf charts showing CPLQ (Liquidity)\n\nHi Alex\n\nIf you don't mind, I wrote many comments on your charts.","a":"Ashkan","d":"","n":"#308","p":13,"im":["118a29fded6085d52dcf6a9f025be898f0b62cff","0e4873187835cfefcf900b45b58c91f14702cd0c"],"m":308},{"id":"aboutcompression_p13_309","t":"Compression in M30 from 10/8 NY session","a":"Nosbigs","d":"","n":"#309","p":13,"im":["81b5d7189307afcbeb0d05f25327dd880fc00e9d"],"m":309},{"id":"aboutcompression_p13_310","t":"Compression in M30 from 10/8 NY session","a":"Nosbigs","d":"","n":"#310","p":13,"im":["81b5d7189307afcbeb0d05f25327dd880fc00e9d"],"m":310},{"id":"aboutcompression_p13_311","t":"I just drew in the cp and s/d pertaining to a possible long set up on cable daily.","a":"Oedipus99","d":"","n":"#311","p":13,"im":["338ab40aeed3954fc74caf0006c219f92977ad8e"],"m":311},{"id":"aboutcompression_p13_312","t":"Another possibility. H4 usd/cad.","a":"Oedipus99","d":"","n":"#312","p":13,"im":["73a9a2f2f9618cbd0bf628a53b5f72ace7634468"],"m":312},{"id":"aboutcompression_p13_313","t":"I noticed some compression zones when marked from htf charts don't transfer to ltfs, candle wise. Glad you pointed these out and for the shorter S/D zones that came up too. Thanks for your help, Ashkan.:)>-","a":"AlexC","d":"","n":"#313","p":13,"im":[],"m":313},{"id":"aboutcompression_p13_314","t":"","a":"Nosbigs","d":"","n":"#314","p":13,"im":["330a9782f410f4c579e01baa4ad9e70875a89d97"],"m":314},{"id":"aboutcompression_p13_315","t":"I find that my download stalls at 94% and therefore fails My issue? with my computers am really struggling with this concept\n\noutapips wrote: Hi IF,\n\nI'm having problems trying to read the compression book.. each time I click on it I get and error page coming up saying not found.. I also tried to click on link whiteout put in reply to me and I'm guessing its back to the same place as it comes up with an error too.\n\nCan you check for me please?\n\nThx","a":"Nosbigs","d":"","n":"#315","p":13,"im":[],"m":315},{"id":"aboutcompression_p13_316","t":"Checked right now Nos, rapidshare work, multiulpoad work, scribd too. link 1 link 2 link 3 feel free to pm me if y still have problem. anyway, that document is a 1.0, there will be a better an inproved 2.0 version.","a":"whiteout","d":"","n":"#316","p":13,"im":[],"m":316},{"id":"aboutcompression_p13_317","t":"still not working, something wrong with all the links...tried almost all of them","a":"extremerrage","d":"","n":"#317","p":13,"im":[],"m":317},{"id":"aboutcompression_p13_318","t":"nooo sorry it worked again...from scribd","a":"extremerrage","d":"","n":"#318","p":13,"im":[],"m":318},{"id":"aboutcompression_p13_319","t":"I realized I didn't really know what compression looked like or did so I'm gonna do some more.","a":"Oedipus99","d":"","n":"#319","p":13,"im":["06f42d73568a57fe2e2630d21c9bd29c7e782964"],"m":319},{"id":"aboutcompression_p13_320","t":"So price compresses up into the top rectangle. It's doing this to clear out all the buy orders left there. This compressed price action is forming a bear flag. Once these buy orders are filled price is able to drop straight through where the buy orders were.\n\nThe bottom rectangle has been historically important for s+r, s/d. So would it be logical to assume that if price again compresses up to it the same thing will happen. It will consume the buy orders and drop?????????\n\nI'm no less confused to be perfectly honest with you.","a":"Oedipus99","d":"","n":"#320","p":13,"im":["9f81d25d4b632814ed3d8f213b4bc3279d686cbd"],"m":320},{"id":"aboutcompression_p13_321","t":"You could see compression in action right now on the eurusd. All the demand orders has been taken out, so way has been cleared for the big drop.","a":"okami","d":"","n":"#321","p":13,"im":["71d9806046d29c5cafa6c6649b6a13615d940fd4"],"m":321},{"id":"aboutcompression_p13_322","t":"AH! Hah! The penny beings to drop. Thank you. So from my rudimentary chart below does it not look like that from here it's more likely to bounce now than drop further?","a":"Oedipus99","d":"","n":"#322","p":13,"im":["83b380bd60bed8033014460d8b00645e8a175b50"],"m":322},{"id":"aboutcompression_p13_323","t":"Hello Oedipus.\n\nSomeone can correct me as I haven't yet done the homework but my understanding of CP is that price will spike upwards in a down move (lower lows) i.e clearing supply for a potential move back up, and spike downwards in an up move (higher highs) i.e. clearing demand for a potential move back down...\n\nSo in your diagram above your diagonal line would better placed above price for a downward compression.\n\nWhere you have asked \"Is this cp?\" - I would say no. It's price reacting to the demand level to the left. Whether it will hold is another question:)","a":"snebucA","d":"","n":"#323","p":13,"im":[],"m":323},{"id":"aboutcompression_p13_324","t":"snebucA, yes, you're right about what CP is, and looking to the tops for a downward cp and vice versa\n\nOedipus, where you ask is this CP; there's no sign of it there - that's simply price reacting to the base of the BUFL - Is it rejection or consumption? PA will tell","a":"Ifmyante","d":"","n":"#324","p":13,"im":[],"m":324},{"id":"aboutcompression_p13_325","t":"AH! I see. NO, no I don't. Let me have another look. \"Is it rejection or consumption? PA will tell\". Could you elaborate?\n\n10111213141516","a":"Oedipus99","d":"","n":"#325","p":13,"im":[],"m":325}],"images":[{"k":"563075d2a02cafb879dc4e37fa1c367bd1c450bc","t":"assets/thumbs/563075d2a02cafb879dc4e37fa1c367bd1c450bc.webp","f":"assets/images/563075d2a02cafb879dc4e37fa1c367bd1c450bc.png","w":1296,"h":1000,"b":39168,"o":"563075d2a02cafb879dc4e37fa1c367bd1c450bc.png","p":13,"pid":"aboutcompression_p13_301"},{"k":"f8e8822b4aabd1fca38a8bce54b603794e81cacb","t":"assets/thumbs/f8e8822b4aabd1fca38a8bce54b603794e81cacb.webp","f":"assets/images/f8e8822b4aabd1fca38a8bce54b603794e81cacb.png","w":1296,"h":1000,"b":40327,"o":"f8e8822b4aabd1fca38a8bce54b603794e81cacb.png","p":13,"pid":"aboutcompression_p13_302"},{"k":"0c3e5235ec53b5fab5b6422cf08eda98f5517a16","t":"assets/thumbs/0c3e5235ec53b5fab5b6422cf08eda98f5517a16.webp","f":"assets/images/0c3e5235ec53b5fab5b6422cf08eda98f5517a16.png","w":1296,"h":1000,"b":55565,"o":"0c3e5235ec53b5fab5b6422cf0